y biopsy or ANCA testing"], "alarm_features": ["Severe hyperglycemia (glucose > 500 mg/dL)", "Systemic constitutional symptoms (fatigue, malaise)", "Painful rash in dermatomal distribution", "Abdominal pain and diarrhea", "Smoking + obesity as risk factors"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Endocrine Tumor with Paraneoplastic Skin Lesions", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.586153693790311, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Extremely elevated glucose consistent with paraneoplastic hyperglycemia (e.g., glucagonoma), with a threshold >500 mg/dL being rare in metabolic syndrome alone. This provides moderate support for B1.", "The absence of classical metabolic syndrome features (e.g., acanthosis nigricans, family history of T2DM) and the presence of severe hyperglycemia with paraneoplastic skin findings (unlisted in metabolic syndrome's typical presentations) provides strong against evidence for B2."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Does the rash exhibit features consistent with a paraneoplastic process (e.g., necrolytic migratory erythema)?", "Is there evidence of weight loss or unexplained symptoms of tumor?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Serum glucagon level", "Abdominal/pelvic imaging (CT/MRI)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.65, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Metabolic Syndrome with Severe Hyperglycemia", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.12109772493237327, "danger": 0.45, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of classical metabolic syndrome features (e.g., acanthosis nigricans, family history of T2DM) and the presence of severe hyperglycemia with paraneoplastic skin findings (unlisted in metabolic syndrome's typical presentations) provides strong against evidence for B2."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Hypercortisolism-Related Endocrine Syndrome", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.06854479340252177, "danger": 0.65, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The description of a painful erythematous/pustular rash contrasts with Cushing syndrome's nonpainful skin manifestations (e.g., striae, ecchymoses). This weakly argues against B3."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Autoimmune Beta Cell Destruction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.08, "posterior": 0.09964612794435286, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is there a history of type 1 diabetes symptoms (e.g., polyuria, polydipsia)?", "Do family members have autoimmune diabetes or other endocrine deficiencies?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["C-peptide suppression testing", "Autoimmune markers (iCA, GADA)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.25, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive Hyperglycemia with Secondary Dermatological Manifestations", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.1, "posterior": 0.12455765993044109, "danger": 0.35, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is the rash improving after glucose normalization?", "Are systemic symptoms linked to a concurrent acute infection?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Inflammatory markers (CRP, ESR)", "Skin biopsy"], "turn