 urination\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, elevated serum creatinine\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Multiple Myeloma:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: anemia, bone pain, constipation, fatigue, frequent urination\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Multiple Myeloma:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: anemia, constipation, frequent urination, hypercalcemia, hyperviscosity syndrome\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Multiple Myeloma:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: anemia, bone pain, constipation, frequent urination, hypercalcemia\n\nRelated to Leukemoid Reaction (Reactive Leukocytosis): plasma 