ss/ataxia or cranial nerve signs)", "Metabolic decompensation (diabetic): less likely given the blasts and constitutional signs rather than acute metabolic derangement", "Infectious myelopathy: possible but pancytopenia with blasts raises higher suspicion for hematological cause first"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional signs (night sweats, fever, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blasts", "Nonfocal neurological signs in context of systemic disease"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.3561094098626208, "posterior": 0.9824762153116207, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["35% blasts + pancytopenia with subacute constitutional symptoms strongly suggest acute myeloid leukemia over lymphoid or chronic processes. High blasts are typical for AML but atypical for CML or ALL in this context.", "Lack of chronic leukocytosis/splenomegaly in the vignette argues against chronic myeloproliferative disorders like CML, favoring acute leukemia (AML/ALL) as the presentation is more compatible with immediate bone marrow failure."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Are blasts morphologically myeloid or lymphoid?", "Does the bone marrow biopsy show dysplasia or fibrosis?", "Is there a history of chronic myeloproliferative disease?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Flow cytometry for blast lineage characterization", "Bone marrow aspiration and biopsy", "Cytogenetic analysis (e.g., Philadelphia chromosome testing)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "test_pathway"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.004329676508197271, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of splenomegaly or prior leukocytosis provides strong evidence against CML in blast crisis."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.004329676508197271, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of splenomegaly or prior leukocytosis provides strong evidence against CML in blast crisis."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.003008531706596683, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of splenomegaly or prior leukocytosis provides strong evidence against CML in blast crisis."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0008742944749227607, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["35% blasts + pancytopenia with subacute constitutional symptoms strongly suggest acute myeloid leukemia over lymphoid or chronic processes. High blasts are typical for AML but atypical for CML or ALL in this context."]}, "B6": {"id": "B6", "label": "Other Mass", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0025284553916632736, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3004673145715863, "posterior": 0.27334313630502516, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Absence of multilineage dysplasia in the lab findings provides weak evidence against MDS with excess blasts.", "Complete absence of chronic CML features (BCR-ABL negativity, no prior CML history) provides strong evidence