myelodysplastic morphology or lineage abnormalities) effectively refute MDS with excess blasts as the cause in favor of de novo AML?", "result_summary": "Absence of dysplasia documentation in the lab results provides weak evidence against MDS with excess blasts.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "weak_for", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "weak_against", "B6.3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of chronic CML markers (prior leukocytosis, splenomegaly) effectively rule out CML in blast crisis as the systemic cause of leukocytosis, pancytopenia, and nonfocal neurological symptoms?", "result_summary": "Absence of splenomegaly or prior leukocytosis provides strong evidence against CML in blast crisis.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "moderate_for", "B2": "strong_against", "B3": "strong_against", "B4": "strong_against", "B1.2": "strong_against", "B1.3": "neutral", "B6.3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Would the lack of mention of multilineage dysplasia in the presented findings strongly contradict myelodysplastic syndrome (MDS) as the cause of blasts and pancytopenia, favoring de novo AML?", "result_summary": "Absence of multilineage dysplasia in the lab findings provides weak evidence against MDS with excess blasts.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "weak_for", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B1.3": "weak_against", "B6.3": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 5, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the complete absence of chronic CML features (prior splenomegaly, BCR-ABL positivity